1. whoami: Displays current username
2. hostname: Displays system hostname
3. pwd (present working directory): Displays the current working directory.

4. ls: List all the files and directories.
     ls -l : Displays detailed file information.
     ls -lt: Lists files by modification time.
     ls -a : Displays hidden files.
     ls -lr: 

5. mkdir : Creates directory
6. mkdir -p : Creates nested directories
7. rmdir: Removes empty directory
8. cd:   Changes directory 	         -- cd /home
9. cd .. : Moves to parent directory     -- cd ..

10. touch: Creates an empty file
11. cat: Displays file content
12. more: Views file content page by page
13. less: Views file page by page
14. head: Displays first 10 lines
15. tail: Displays last 10 lines
16. cp:   Copies files
17. mv: Moves or renames files
18. rm: Removes files
19. rm -r: Removes directories recursively
20. file: Identifies file type
